{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumCut"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"capacity"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:5Flows3CutV","identifier":"doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/Cut","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Cut"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols12DirectedViewV","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedView","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"DirectedView"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":">? "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s18AdditiveArithmeticP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AdditiveArithmetic"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Comparable"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The cut minimizes the capacity of the edges between a nonempty proper vertex set and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rest. The side holding the first vertex is the source side. Computed by Nagamochi–Ibaraki:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"maximum adjacency orderings that contract every edge whose scanned connection is at least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the best cut so far. Which minimum cut is returned when several exist is unspecified, but"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same input always gives the same cut."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the edges of positive capacity do not connect the graph, the result is the cut of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value zero whose source side is the first vertex’s component, with every crossing edge."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Parallel capacities add and self-loops are ignored. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity"},{"type":"text","text":" is called once per non-loop"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge, in position order, before any work."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Sums are formed in a wider type than ","type":"text"},{"code":"C","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" where needed (","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int128","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for fixed-width","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"integers, ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for ","type":"text"},{"code":"Float","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), so a contracted group’s connection may exceed ","type":"text"},{"code":"C","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s range.","type":"text"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(nm log n) in the worst case."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Complexity"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every capacity is at least zero, not NaN and finite, and the minimum cut’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value fits in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"C"},{"text":" (it is at most every vertex’s capacity sum).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Precondition"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/flows\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumcut(capacity:)"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A global minimum cut over "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"directedView"},{"type":"text","text":", or nil below two vertices."}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","title":"minimumCut(capacity:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumCut","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"capacity","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:5Flows3CutV","text":"Cut","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols12DirectedViewV","text":"DirectedView","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Flows","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5FlowsE10minimumCut8capacityAD0E0VyAA12DirectedViewVyxGqd__GSgqd__5Edges_5IndexQZXE_ts18AdditiveArithmeticRd_